        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "{\"output\":\"=== README.md ===\\n# Service component\\n\\nFix transfer(connection, publisher, source, target, amount) in src/service.py. A successful transfer debits and credits exactly once, appends one ledger row, commits, then publishes {'source': source, 'target': target, 'amount': amount}. source and target must differ and exist; amount is a positive integer, excluding bool, and cannot exceed the source balance. Invalid transfers raise ValueError without writes or publication. Database failure at any statement or commit rolls back all changes and never publishes. Publication failure propagates after the committed transfer and must not undo it. Caller connections are idle at entry. Keep balance reads and account setup intact. Start in src/service.py and src/repository.py.\\n\\nRun `python3 checks/public.py` from the project root. Implementation belongs in src/. Add checks under checks/.\\n\\n=== checks/public.py ===\\nimport os, sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, os.getcwd())\\nimport sqlite3\\nfrom src.repository import initialize, balance\\nfrom src.service import transfer\\nfrom src.events import Recorder\\nc = sqlite3.connect(\\\":memory:\\\")\\ninitialize(c)\\nc.executemany(\\\"INSERT INTO accounts VALUES (?, ?)\\\", [(\\\"a\\\", 100), (\\\"b\\\", 20)])\\nc.commit()\\np = Recorder()\\ntransfer(c, p, \\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", 10)\\nassert (balance(c, \\\"a\\\"), balance(c, \\\"b\\\")) == (90, 30)\\nassert p.events == [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"a\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"b\\\", \\\"amount\\\": 10}]\\n\\n=== src/events.py ===\\nclass Recorder:\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self.events = []\\n\\n    def publish(self, event):\\n        self.events.append(event.copy())\\n\\n=== src/__init__.py ===\\n(end __init__)\\n=== checks dir ===\\nchecks:\\ntotal 4\\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 501 dialout  96 Oct 11 20:38 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 501 dialout 160 Oct 11 20:38 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 501 dialout 472 Oct 11 20:38 public.py\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"signal\":null,\"cancelled\":false,\"timeout\":false,\"truncated\":false}"
